---
globs:
  - "artifacts/**/*.json"
  - "workflow/**/*.md"
alwaysApply: true
---

Default B1 (`FB_DRAFT_MODE=true`, chat or Drive): do **not** open the local
review page. After explicit chat confirmation and enough images, create a Meta
unpublished draft with `npm run meta:publish -- --draft <post_job_id>`. The
Page admin reviews and publishes on Facebook; that click is the final
decision. Chat still cannot make a post public. The agent never writes or
edits `approval.json`.

Live path only when `FB_DRAFT_MODE` is unset: an approval is valid only for
the exact content hash, selected variant, asset IDs, Page ID, and any per-post
quality override shown to the reviewer. The chat draft must be materialized
into the local review profile before the preview is opened. Any edit creates a
new version and invalidates approval. AI may prepare `NEEDS_HUMAN_APPROVAL`;
only the local review server (`backend/approval/local-review-server.mjs`)
signing `approval.json` with `APPROVAL_SIGNING_KEY` may create `APPROVED`.
The decision is always a button click on the local review page opened by
`npm run review:open -- <post_job_id>`; a chat message, an `AskQuestion`
selection, or silence is never a decision. The agent must never write or edit
`approval.json` by hand, never infer approval, and never choose "Duyệt và
đăng" for the reviewer.
